      "style": "prismworks",
      "focal_face": "north",
      "narrative": "A stair tower of polished blackstone and smooth basalt beside the Prism Ascent: a pier rhythm broken by four courses of barred window at every storey, a string course at every floor, a corbelled oversail under the crown, an open loggia on the west face at the fourth storey, and a deck sixty-five courses over the lawn with a parapet, four lit corner piers and open sky. At the first storey a single cell of deck crosses onto the Prism Ascent's podium roof, which has been standing unreachable since it was built.\n"
